<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Kubernetes-Yaml-파일로-동적-값을-설정하는-방법 on K-Life Hack | Systems Architecture &amp; DevOps</title><link>https://klifehack.com/en/tags/kubernetes-yaml-%ED%8C%8C%EC%9D%BC%EB%A1%9C-%EB%8F%99%EC%A0%81-%EA%B0%92%EC%9D%84-%EC%84%A4%EC%A0%95%ED%95%98%EB%8A%94-%EB%B0%A9%EB%B2%95/</link><description>Recent content in Kubernetes-Yaml-파일로-동적-값을-설정하는-방법 on K-Life Hack | Systems Architecture &amp; DevOps</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:30:22 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://klifehack.com/en/tags/kubernetes-yaml-%ED%8C%8C%EC%9D%BC%EB%A1%9C-%EB%8F%99%EC%A0%81-%EA%B0%92%EC%9D%84-%EC%84%A4%EC%A0%95%ED%95%98%EB%8A%94-%EB%B0%A9%EB%B2%95/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Methods for Defining Secret Resources in Kubernetes and Injecting Environment Variables into Pods</title><link>https://klifehack.com/en/p/k8s-secret-management-pod-environment/</link><pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:30:22 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://klifehack.com/en/p/k8s-secret-management-pod-environment/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="secure-management-and-configuration-methods-for-sensitive-information-using-kubernetes-secret-objects"&gt;Secure Management and Configuration Methods for Sensitive Information Using Kubernetes Secret Objects
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Meta Description&lt;/b&gt;: This article explains isolated management of sensitive information using Secret objects in Kubernetes, generation procedures via CLI/YAML, injection patterns into Pods, Base64 encoding caveats, and troubleshooting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In container environments, hardcoding sensitive information such as database connection strings and authentication tokens into application source code or container images poses significant security risks. In Kubernetes, while non-sensitive configurations are managed using ConfigMaps, sensitive data such as credentials and encryption keys are managed separately as Secret objects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By using Secret objects, configuration data is decoupled from application logic, allowing configurations to be securely deployed to Pods as environment variables or volumes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="methods-for-generating-secret-objects"&gt;Methods for Generating Secret Objects
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Methods for defining Secrets in Kubernetes include declarative/imperative approaches via CLI commands and approaches using YAML manifests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="generation-via-cli-imperative-commands"&gt;Generation via CLI Imperative Commands
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Using the kubectl create secret command allows direct creation of Secrets without manually encoding data. By using the &amp;ndash;from-literal flag, Base64 encoding is performed automatically by the system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Configuration for registering a single value:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl create secret generic app-secret --from-literal&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;DB_HOST&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;mysql
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Configuration for registering multiple connection details together:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl create secret generic app-secret &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; --from-literal&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;DB_HOST&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;mysql &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; --from-literal&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;DB_USER&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;root &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; --from-literal&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;DB_PASSWORD&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;passwrd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="generation-from-property-files"&gt;Generation from Property Files
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;When an existing property file (e.g., app_secret.properties) is present, it can be batch-converted into a Secret using the &amp;ndash;from-file flag. In this case, the file name is automatically mapped as the Key, and the file contents as the Value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Target file configuration (app_secret.properties):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-properties" data-lang="properties"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;DB_HOST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;mysql&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;DB_USER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;DB_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;passwrd&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Execution command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl create secret generic app-secret --from-file&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;app_secret.properties
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="declarative-definition-via-yaml-manifests"&gt;Declarative Definition via YAML Manifests
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;When integrating into GitOps or CI/CD pipelines, definition via YAML files is standard. When writing configurations in the data field of a YAML manifest, the values must be pre-encoded in Base64.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base64 encoding process (Linux/Unix environment):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo -n &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;mysql&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64 &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Output example: bXlzcWw=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo -n &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;root&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64 &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Output example: cm9vdA==&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo -n &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;passwrd&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64 &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Output example: cGFzc3dyZA==&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Manifest definition (secret-data.yaml):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;apiVersion&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;v1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;Secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;app-secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;Opaque&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;DB_HOST&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;bXlzcWw=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;DB_USER&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;cm9vdA==&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;DB_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;cGFzc3dyZA==&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deployment execution:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl apply -f secret-data.yaml
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="inspecting-and-decoding-secrets"&gt;Inspecting and Decoding Secrets
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use the following commands to check the state of deployed Secrets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Retrieving the list of registered Secrets:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl get secrets
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Inspecting Secret metadata (*note: actual values are masked when displayed):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl describe secret app-secret
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To check raw encoded data:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl get secret app-secret -o yaml
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;To decode and verify the retrieved Base64 string back into plain text, execute base64 &amp;ndash;decode.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo -n &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;bXlzcWw=&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64 --decode
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="configuration-for-injecting-secrets-into-pods"&gt;Configuration for Injecting Secrets into Pods
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The created Secret can be injected into Pod containers as environment variables. Base64 is automatically decoded internally by Kubernetes, making it accessible to the containerized application as standard plain text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="batch-injection-of-all-keys-as-environment-variables-envfrom"&gt;Batch Injection of All Keys as Environment Variables (envFrom)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Configuration example for loading all key-value pairs in a Secret into container environment variables:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;apiVersion&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;v1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;Pod&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;labels&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;spec&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;containers&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;ports&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;containerPort&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;8080&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;envFrom&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;secretRef&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;app-secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id="selecting-and-injecting-specific-keys-secretkeyref"&gt;Selecting and Injecting Specific Keys (secretKeyRef)
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Configuration example for selecting specific keys and mapping them to specific environment variable names:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;apiVersion&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;v1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;Pod&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;metadata&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;spec&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;containers&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;image&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;simple-webapp-color&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;env&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; - &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;DB_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;valueFrom&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;secretKeyRef&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;app-secret&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;DB_PASSWORD&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="troubleshooting"&gt;Troubleshooting
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Several typical configuration errors can occur during the creation and operation of Secrets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-1-trailing-newline-character-inclusion-during-base64-encoding"&gt;🛠️ 1. Trailing Newline Character Inclusion During Base64 Encoding
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;⚠️ When performing Base64 encoding with the echo command, omitting the -n option will encode the data with an included newline character (\n).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Incorrect example (includes a newline)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;passwrd&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Output: cGFzc3dyZAo=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Correct example&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;echo -n &lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;passwrd&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; | base64
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Output: cGFzc3dyZA==&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Generating a Secret with a trailing newline character included can cause password mismatch errors (Authentication Failed) when the application attempts to connect to the database.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-2-reflection-limitations-of-dynamic-updates-in-environment-variable-injection"&gt;🛠️ 2. Reflection Limitations of Dynamic Updates in Environment Variable Injection
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Secret values loaded via a Pod&amp;rsquo;s env or envFrom fields are passed to the process at the time the Pod starts. Therefore, even if the values of the Secret object are modified later using kubectl edit secret or similar commands, environment variables inside running Pods will not be updated automatically.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To apply updated configurations, a rolling update must be executed, or the Pods must be restarted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;kubectl rollout restart deployment &amp;lt;deployment-name&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="execution-verification-log-protocol"&gt;Execution Verification Log Protocol
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Command-line output example verifying that the Secret is properly decoded and injected into environment variables after the Pod has started:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ kubectl get secret app-secret
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NAME TYPE DATA AGE
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;app-secret Opaque 3 5m12s
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ kubectl exec simple-webapp-color -- printenv | grep DB_
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;DB_HOST=mysql
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;DB_USER=root
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;DB_PASSWORD=passwrd
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="configuration-notes"&gt;Configuration Notes
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 Note that standard Kubernetes Secrets are merely &amp;ldquo;Base64 encoded&amp;rdquo;, not &amp;ldquo;encrypted&amp;rdquo;. To encrypt them when stored in etcd itself, you must configure EncryptionConfiguration on the Kube-apiserver side or consider integrating with external secret management tools (such as HashiCorp Vault).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💡 When registering Secret resource definition manifests (YAML) in a Git repository, it is recommended to manage them in an encrypted state using tools such as SOPS (Secrets Opaque Secret) or Sealed Secrets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/deployment-name&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>